<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's net reserves down to $1.72 bln by Dec 6.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's net reserves down to $1.72 bln by Dec 6.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Monday its net international reserves stood at $1.72 billion on December 6, down $72 million from the week before.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.56 billion at the end of last year, down $145 million from the end of 1994.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
